  "body": "`crates/motion/tests/` has 120 integration test binaries (119 flat files and 1 directory suite `rest_adaptive`), taking 4.03 GB for one target set and 21.0 s for a warm crate build on Linux (`-j 6`).\n\nFold the 117 non-slow suites into ~10–12 domain directory suites (`machining2d`, `turning`, `machining3d`, `finishing3d`, `multiaxis`, `drilling`, `entry_links`, `cl_laws`, and similar balanced groups). Keep the 3 `SLOW_BINARIES` (`motion:finish3d`, `motion:pivot5d`, `motion:flow` in `xtask/src/plan.rs`) as separate binaries so `gate batch` still skips them and `gate release` still runs them. Keep `#[ignore]` heavy tests and Gate maps intact.\n\nExpected saving: ~3.6 GB disk per worktree (-89%) and ~12 s warm build on Linux (~35 s on Windows), plus faster release heavy builds.\n\nDepends on the `xtask` directory-suite prerequisite (Part of #919).\n\nEvidence and measurements: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-7065686766\n\nDone means: `crates/motion/tests/` has at most 16 binaries, `SLOW_BINARIES` and `#[test]` counts (normal and ignored) stay unchanged, and `cargo xtask gate batch` passes.\n\nPart of #919\n",
